Per the FCC docs.. *the device is '''MediaTek''' based *and running Android *'''Hynix''' NAND Flash + RAM *the device supports the following cellular bands... **GSM (850/900/1800/1900MHz) **UMTS (900/2100MHz) *the device supports single-stream 802.11n *Micro USB charging / data port *per the label, the device uses a 90:5F:2E WiFi and BT OUI
